1
00:00:07,674 --> 00:00:09,968
[creaking]

2
00:00:21,187 --> 00:00:23,189
[fluttering]

3
00:00:23,273 --> 00:00:24,899
[creature screeches distantly]

4
00:00:34,034 --> 00:00:38,830
Please, my lord, let no harm come to me.
Give me some streng--

5
00:00:38,913 --> 00:00:41,541
Hey, quit that now. Come and help me here!

6
00:00:42,417 --> 00:00:43,501
[whimpers]

7
00:00:48,214 --> 00:00:49,048
Hey!

8
00:00:50,300 --> 00:00:51,801
Motherfuckers!

9
00:00:51,885 --> 00:00:54,929
When I get out of here,
I'm gonna kill all of you.

10
00:00:57,265 --> 00:00:59,684
What do you bastards want with me?

11
00:00:59,768 --> 00:01:01,853
Let me out of here, you assholes!

12
00:01:01,936 --> 00:01:03,980
Come on! What is it you want?

13
00:01:05,607 --> 00:01:06,816
Motherfuckers.

14
00:01:08,109 --> 00:01:10,528
[whimpering]

15
00:01:10,612 --> 00:01:13,364
[whimpers, mumbles]

16
00:01:13,448 --> 00:01:14,532
[screams]

17
00:01:14,616 --> 00:01:17,243
[man 1] Let me go.
Will you get your hands off me? [groans]

18
00:01:17,327 --> 00:01:19,913
Dear lord, let no harm come to me here.

19
00:01:19,996 --> 00:01:22,040
[man 2] I beseech you…

20
00:01:22,123 --> 00:01:23,333
[grunts]

21
00:01:26,669 --> 00:01:30,215
[splutters] Where are you taking me?
You motherfuckers, let me go!

22
00:01:30,298 --> 00:01:33,593
Let me go, you bastards! Oh my god…

23
00:01:38,723 --> 00:01:40,141
[ominous music playing]

24
00:01:40,225 --> 00:01:41,518
[panting]

25
00:01:48,733 --> 00:01:49,943
Hey.

26
00:01:50,026 --> 00:01:52,403
That one, they've taken him away.

27
00:01:52,487 --> 00:01:54,114
[creature screeches distantly]

28
00:01:55,949 --> 00:01:57,367
[sniffs]

29
00:02:01,996 --> 00:02:03,206
[grunts]

30
00:02:13,925 --> 00:02:14,926
Come on!

31
00:02:16,511 --> 00:02:18,179
Come on. Aren't you coming?

32
00:02:32,777 --> 00:02:34,696
[man 1] Help!

33
00:02:36,531 --> 00:02:38,867
- [breathes loudly]
- [man 1] No!

34
00:02:42,745 --> 00:02:45,039
[man 1] Somebody help me!

35
00:02:47,041 --> 00:02:49,043
[panting]

36
00:02:49,127 --> 00:02:51,129
[tense music playing]

37
00:03:06,394 --> 00:03:08,396
[panting]

38
00:03:14,777 --> 00:03:16,779
[loud creaking]

39
00:03:20,783 --> 00:03:23,453
- [creature growling]
- [whimpering]

40
00:03:27,707 --> 00:03:29,334
[panting]

41
00:03:35,965 --> 00:03:37,383
[creature screeches distantly]

42
00:03:37,467 --> 00:03:39,469
[whimpering]

43
00:03:43,348 --> 00:03:45,350
[ominous music playing]

44
00:04:04,327 --> 00:04:05,828
[yelling] Hey!

45
00:04:08,122 --> 00:04:09,123
Help me!

46
00:04:12,919 --> 00:04:14,921
[panting]

47
00:04:34,983 --> 00:04:36,609
[man 2 pants]

48
00:04:46,286 --> 00:04:48,288
[panting, whimpering]

49
00:04:54,627 --> 00:04:56,087
[cries]

50
00:04:59,716 --> 00:05:02,719
[cries loudly]

51
00:05:10,810 --> 00:05:12,812
[theme music playing]

52
00:06:16,918 --> 00:06:20,338
BALARAW: BLOOD ISLAND

53
00:06:38,022 --> 00:06:38,898
Ma?

54
00:06:40,608 --> 00:06:42,235
We have to leave now, okay?

55
00:06:43,277 --> 00:06:44,695
Oh. Why so soon?

56
00:06:46,572 --> 00:06:48,324
This is your first ever job.

57
00:06:48,407 --> 00:06:50,451
You… You can't afford to be late.

58
00:06:50,535 --> 00:06:52,620
I don't start until the afternoon.

59
00:06:53,454 --> 00:06:54,705
First, we'll eat.

60
00:06:54,789 --> 00:06:55,706
Let's go.

61
00:06:58,417 --> 00:07:01,462
[door opens, closes]

62
00:07:31,993 --> 00:07:33,619
[soft tense music plays]

63
00:07:48,426 --> 00:07:50,845
Hey, I thought you quit that.

64
00:08:10,364 --> 00:08:11,491
[car engine starts]

65
00:08:12,241 --> 00:08:13,367
[tires screech]

66
00:08:25,796 --> 00:08:26,964
Ma.

67
00:08:28,299 --> 00:08:30,510
Are you still dreaming about the island?

68
00:08:36,015 --> 00:08:36,933
Mmm.

69
00:08:39,852 --> 00:08:40,686
Why?

70
00:08:42,104 --> 00:08:45,107
That man in the photograph…

71
00:08:46,526 --> 00:08:48,528
Does he still appear to you
at night in your dreams?

72
00:08:53,616 --> 00:08:54,450
Yes, he does.

73
00:08:56,577 --> 00:08:58,496
He's always being chased by someone,

74
00:08:58,579 --> 00:09:01,582
but the dream always ends
just before he's caught.

75
00:09:02,625 --> 00:09:04,293
Is this the man running?

76
00:09:12,677 --> 00:09:15,680
Ma, why do you keep asking?
Who is he anyway?

77
00:09:19,809 --> 00:09:21,060
And you've never told me

78
00:09:21,644 --> 00:09:23,980
the reason I keep having
these dreams that bother you.

79
00:09:24,063 --> 00:09:25,523
Don't they bother you?

80
00:09:27,191 --> 00:09:29,026
Ma, this is my first day at work.

81
00:09:29,110 --> 00:09:31,112
Can you not stress me out like this?

82
00:09:37,493 --> 00:09:39,579
I know you can look after yourself.

83
00:09:44,000 --> 00:09:45,459
Ma, why are you…

84
00:09:45,543 --> 00:09:47,044
[cell phone ringing]

85
00:09:48,629 --> 00:09:50,047
[cell phone continues ringing]

86
00:09:50,131 --> 00:09:51,215
You should answer.

87
00:09:53,175 --> 00:09:54,176
[cell phone stops ringing]

88
00:10:01,809 --> 00:10:03,311
Eventually, you'll understand.

89
00:10:08,524 --> 00:10:10,943
- [cell phone ringing]
- [Sabina sighs]

90
00:10:20,202 --> 00:10:23,456
[Bulak] <i>Babe, I need your help.</i>
<i>Arturo is nagging at me again.</i>

91
00:10:23,539 --> 00:10:25,875
<i>Can you get your mom</i>
<i>to have a talk with him?</i>

92
00:10:25,958 --> 00:10:28,669
<i>He'll believe her if she says I'm clean.</i>

93
00:10:28,753 --> 00:10:29,962
It's not that easy.

94
00:10:31,130 --> 00:10:33,341
Mom's kind of stressed out right now.

95
00:10:33,424 --> 00:10:35,635
[Bulak] <i>Huh? Is she okay or what?</i>

96
00:10:36,260 --> 00:10:38,471
[sighs] You know how she gets.

97
00:10:40,640 --> 00:10:43,684
You just lie low for now.
I'll have a talk with him.

98
00:10:43,768 --> 00:10:44,810
[Bulak] <i>Okay. Thank you.</i>

99
00:10:50,691 --> 00:10:51,609
[sighs]

100
00:11:02,620 --> 00:11:04,622
[horns honking distantly]

101
00:11:05,581 --> 00:11:07,583
[sinister music playing]

102
00:11:17,385 --> 00:11:19,470
[waitress] Hello. Shall I bring the bill?

103
00:11:19,553 --> 00:11:21,764
[customer]
Yes, it was very nice. Thank you.

104
00:11:31,190 --> 00:11:33,943
Pardon me. Did you see
where the woman I was with went?

105
00:11:34,610 --> 00:11:36,362
I think she went for a smoke.

106
00:11:39,907 --> 00:11:41,909
[horns honking]

107
00:11:45,329 --> 00:11:46,664
[horn honking]

108
00:11:51,585 --> 00:11:54,588
[horns honking]

109
00:12:10,354 --> 00:12:12,189
[truck engine revs]

110
00:12:17,820 --> 00:12:20,322
[male reporter] <i>We're monitoring</i>
<i>the ongoing situation here…</i>

111
00:12:20,406 --> 00:12:21,323
[bell ringing]

112
00:12:21,407 --> 00:12:23,033
<i>…as locals prepare to evacuate,</i>

113
00:12:23,117 --> 00:12:26,328
<i>following flooding</i>
<i>and the ensuing landslides.</i>

114
00:12:26,412 --> 00:12:29,248
<i>Reporting live from the town of Mariano.</i>

115
00:12:29,331 --> 00:12:33,043
<i>Back to Ero Francisco</i>
<i>in the studio now. Ero?</i>

116
00:12:33,127 --> 00:12:36,297
[Ero] <i>The typhoon hit</i>
<i>the town of Mariano late last night.</i>

117
00:12:36,380 --> 00:12:39,800
<i>Officials estimate</i>
<i>the storm has affected the livelihoods</i>

118
00:12:39,884 --> 00:12:43,512
<i>of at least 60 fishing families</i>
<i>in the local villages.</i>

119
00:12:43,596 --> 00:12:45,806
<i>At this point,</i>
<i>the situation remains critical.</i>

120
00:12:45,890 --> 00:12:46,807
[knock at door]

121
00:12:46,891 --> 00:12:49,101
<i>Local fishing boats are remaining in port</i>

122
00:12:49,185 --> 00:12:52,188
<i>due to this seemingly</i>
<i>never-ending downpour.</i>

123
00:12:52,271 --> 00:12:55,107
<i>This is Ero Francisco reporting.</i>
<i>Back to you, Ali.</i>

124
00:12:55,191 --> 00:12:56,192
[knocking at door]

125
00:12:56,275 --> 00:12:58,944
[Ali] <i>Coordination is ongoing</i>
<i>throughout Metro Manila…</i>

126
00:12:59,028 --> 00:12:59,945
[knocking at door]

127
00:13:00,029 --> 00:13:03,949
<i>…and authorities are currently monitoring</i>
<i>the ongoing flood situation</i>

128
00:13:04,033 --> 00:13:08,329
<i>and are preparing to evacuate residents</i>
<i>if the situation worsens.</i>

129
00:13:08,412 --> 00:13:09,246
[Bulak] Sabina?

130
00:13:09,330 --> 00:13:11,957
[Ali] <i>Reporting to you live</i>
<i>on this developing crisis…</i>

131
00:13:12,041 --> 00:13:12,875
[Bulak] Babe?

132
00:13:12,958 --> 00:13:14,877
<i>…which has struck</i>
<i>the fishing village of Mariano.</i>

133
00:13:18,130 --> 00:13:19,882
[knocking at door]

134
00:13:22,301 --> 00:13:25,137
[knocking continues]

135
00:13:28,766 --> 00:13:29,683
[Bulak] Babe.

136
00:13:43,447 --> 00:13:46,075
Babe, are you okay? What happened?

137
00:13:47,076 --> 00:13:50,079
Nothing. [sighs] I just couldn't sleep.

138
00:13:52,289 --> 00:13:55,709
You stayed up watching
the CCTV video, didn't you?

139
00:13:57,378 --> 00:13:59,588
[breathes deeply]

140
00:14:02,174 --> 00:14:04,176
There could be something I didn't see.

141
00:14:06,845 --> 00:14:09,056
If you want, I can watch it again.

142
00:14:09,974 --> 00:14:13,477
Even though I've seen it dozens of times.
It might help. Who knows?

143
00:14:14,186 --> 00:14:15,271
[chuckles softly]

144
00:14:16,480 --> 00:14:17,398
Thank you.

145
00:14:19,358 --> 00:14:20,276
[Sabina] Mmm.

146
00:14:28,075 --> 00:14:32,830
I think we shouldn't waste any more money
on private investigators.

147
00:14:34,373 --> 00:14:36,208
We've spent so much already.

148
00:14:37,960 --> 00:14:41,046
And none of them have found out
anything that's helpful.

149
00:14:44,383 --> 00:14:46,385
Babe, it's been four years now.

150
00:14:47,511 --> 00:14:49,722
Maybe now is the time for you to rest.

151
00:14:50,723 --> 00:14:51,724
Take a break.

152
00:14:52,892 --> 00:14:56,228
Get away from it all.
It could be a really good reset for you.

153
00:14:58,564 --> 00:15:00,900
If you like, we can take a vacation.

154
00:15:00,983 --> 00:15:03,193
After all, we've been planning to do that.

155
00:15:07,239 --> 00:15:10,910
Haven't you forgotten
that I was fired from my job?

156
00:15:12,036 --> 00:15:14,246
[sighs] We don't have any money left.

157
00:15:15,247 --> 00:15:18,167
I will help. I have savings.

158
00:15:25,925 --> 00:15:29,053
It scares me
that if you don't get some rest,

159
00:15:30,387 --> 00:15:32,056
I will lose you forever.

160
00:15:44,652 --> 00:15:46,528
I can't stop. It's too hard.

161
00:15:48,572 --> 00:15:50,783
[breathes deeply]

162
00:15:51,575 --> 00:15:52,576
All I know is…

163
00:15:54,036 --> 00:15:55,663
I need to find my mom.

164
00:15:59,541 --> 00:16:02,628
I know. We're going to find her together.

165
00:16:03,796 --> 00:16:04,880
[Bulak sighs softly]

166
00:16:12,054 --> 00:16:14,682
[Bulak breathes deeply]

167
00:16:20,229 --> 00:16:22,731
[siren wailing distantly]

168
00:16:23,607 --> 00:16:26,610
[nurse 1] That's her.
She's the one who hit the doctor.

169
00:16:26,694 --> 00:16:29,530
- [nurse 2] Why did she hit him?
- [nurse 1] Who knows? Just crazy.

170
00:16:30,572 --> 00:16:33,701
[breathes deeply]

171
00:16:34,618 --> 00:16:36,245
[breathes deeply]

172
00:16:36,328 --> 00:16:39,331
[nurses chatting indistinctly]

173
00:16:40,666 --> 00:16:42,292
I'm here to pick up my salary.

174
00:16:42,376 --> 00:16:43,794
- [cashier] Your name?
- Tejeros.

175
00:16:44,670 --> 00:16:45,879
Tejeros?

176
00:16:45,963 --> 00:16:49,800
Oh, you're the… the nurse
who hit Dr. Gomez.

177
00:16:49,883 --> 00:16:51,969
I want to pick up my last pay.

178
00:16:52,052 --> 00:16:53,429
[paper rustling]

179
00:16:55,055 --> 00:16:56,432
Sign here.

180
00:17:02,855 --> 00:17:04,440
Thank you.

181
00:17:07,568 --> 00:17:08,610
I'll pray for you.

182
00:17:09,194 --> 00:17:11,947
I hope you get through whatever it is
that you're going through.

183
00:17:27,296 --> 00:17:29,840
[motorcycle approaching]

184
00:17:49,026 --> 00:17:52,738
I have this for you,
but first, give me the 5,000 you owe.

185
00:17:52,821 --> 00:17:54,198
What have you got?

186
00:17:54,281 --> 00:17:55,699
You should trust me on this.

187
00:17:56,366 --> 00:17:57,743
This is going to help you.

188
00:17:57,826 --> 00:17:59,745
- Oh, yeah, sure.
- [man] This is a hopeless case.

189
00:17:59,828 --> 00:18:02,539
You should just be glad
that it's not more.

190
00:18:02,623 --> 00:18:05,084
- This wasn't easy to get.
- So what is it?

191
00:18:05,167 --> 00:18:08,253
[scoffs]
It's a video of where your mother went.

192
00:18:09,338 --> 00:18:12,341
I know you're not looking
for my advice, but…

193
00:18:12,424 --> 00:18:16,053
I don't think you should trust the police
handling this stuff one little bit.

194
00:18:18,055 --> 00:18:19,181
- Why?
- [man chuckles]

195
00:18:19,932 --> 00:18:21,850
The person who gave me this said

196
00:18:21,934 --> 00:18:25,229
three years ago,
a police officer took all the CCTV.

197
00:18:25,979 --> 00:18:29,066
And he paid to ensure
that nobody else ever gets a copy.

198
00:18:29,191 --> 00:18:30,734
- It was Arturo.
- [man] Yeah.

199
00:18:31,860 --> 00:18:34,488
I give up thinking
you'll ever see your mother again.

200
00:18:35,322 --> 00:18:38,742
Because she's lost her mind.
You can even see that on this video.

201
00:18:38,826 --> 00:18:40,035
[angrily] Fuck you!

202
00:18:40,828 --> 00:18:43,831
If this isn't what you say it is,
I'll be back for you.

203
00:19:00,097 --> 00:19:01,431
[breathes deeply]

204
00:19:01,515 --> 00:19:03,225
[laptop chimes]

205
00:19:09,982 --> 00:19:11,984
[tense music playing]

206
00:19:12,067 --> 00:19:13,569
[Sabina exhales deeply]

207
00:19:15,779 --> 00:19:17,781
[music builds]

208
00:19:28,667 --> 00:19:30,669
[breathes deeply]

209
00:19:45,434 --> 00:19:47,060
[knock on door]

210
00:19:48,896 --> 00:19:50,314
[knock on door]

211
00:19:52,691 --> 00:19:53,609
[Sabina] Uncle!

212
00:19:56,778 --> 00:19:58,572
- Uncle!
- Yeah?

213
00:19:58,655 --> 00:19:59,948
[knocking continues]

214
00:20:03,869 --> 00:20:05,662
[knock on door]

215
00:20:05,746 --> 00:20:07,247
- [Sabina] Uncle!
- Yeah.

216
00:20:09,416 --> 00:20:10,709
Finally.

217
00:20:11,460 --> 00:20:13,503
It's almost ten o'clock.

218
00:20:14,463 --> 00:20:16,006
[sighs] I fell asleep.

219
00:20:18,884 --> 00:20:20,719
I need to show you something.

220
00:20:22,262 --> 00:20:23,805
Have you eaten dinner yet?

221
00:20:30,145 --> 00:20:32,981
This was taken in Bicol
the day Ma disappeared.

222
00:20:34,483 --> 00:20:36,485
You've seen this before.

223
00:20:44,952 --> 00:20:47,204
No! You answer me.

224
00:20:47,287 --> 00:20:48,372
I told you before,

225
00:20:48,455 --> 00:20:51,959
you're wasting your time
on those shady private investigators.

226
00:20:52,042 --> 00:20:55,128
If I didn't, I wouldn't have found out
what you've been hiding.

227
00:20:57,256 --> 00:20:59,091
Why didn't you tell me about this?

228
00:21:02,344 --> 00:21:03,262
Sabina,

229
00:21:04,763 --> 00:21:08,225
it's <i>all</i> a waste of your time.

230
00:21:08,308 --> 00:21:10,936
She doesn't want you to find her.

231
00:21:11,019 --> 00:21:12,521
So we just give up on her?

232
00:21:16,275 --> 00:21:17,359
[chuckles bitterly]

233
00:21:24,157 --> 00:21:25,075
[Arturo] What?

234
00:21:26,994 --> 00:21:27,828
Sabina?

235
00:21:35,002 --> 00:21:35,877
Give me that!

236
00:21:35,961 --> 00:21:38,130
- No! Give it back to me!
- Sabina!

237
00:21:38,213 --> 00:21:40,340
You might be through looking for her,
but I'm not!

238
00:21:40,424 --> 00:21:41,383
That's enough. Stop.

239
00:21:41,466 --> 00:21:43,468
What else is it
that you're hiding from me?

240
00:21:43,552 --> 00:21:45,387
She doesn't want you to look for her.

241
00:21:47,306 --> 00:21:49,641
If she wanted that,
she would have told you.

242
00:21:50,767 --> 00:21:53,186
It was her decision to leave.
To leave you.

243
00:21:53,270 --> 00:21:54,980
You should learn to accept that.

244
00:21:56,106 --> 00:21:57,774
[both panting]

245
00:21:57,858 --> 00:22:01,069
I didn't tell you because I didn't
want you to follow after her.

246
00:22:03,363 --> 00:22:04,823
I did it to protect you.

247
00:22:10,746 --> 00:22:11,830
Well, thanks a lot.

248
00:22:17,252 --> 00:22:18,462
[door opens]

249
00:22:18,545 --> 00:22:20,380
[rain pattering]

250
00:22:20,464 --> 00:22:22,841
[thunder rumbling]

251
00:22:24,926 --> 00:22:27,429
[Sabina breathes deeply]

252
00:22:30,599 --> 00:22:33,143
[tense music playing]

253
00:23:11,181 --> 00:23:13,767
[Rebecca]
<i>Are you still dreaming about the island?</i>

254
00:23:13,850 --> 00:23:15,560
[music turns sinister]

255
00:23:19,272 --> 00:23:20,982
[music crescendos]

256
00:23:31,201 --> 00:23:32,953
[dogs bark distantly]

257
00:23:39,584 --> 00:23:41,545
[banging]

258
00:23:45,423 --> 00:23:47,759
[dogs continue barking]

259
00:24:27,841 --> 00:24:29,843
[ominous music playing]

260
00:25:04,252 --> 00:25:05,962
[music grows darker]

261
00:25:29,486 --> 00:25:31,738
[keys clacking]

262
00:25:51,758 --> 00:25:53,718
[music crescendos]

263
00:26:19,244 --> 00:26:20,453
[gun cocks]

264
00:27:26,603 --> 00:27:27,437
[Arturo] <i>Sabina.</i>

265
00:27:28,188 --> 00:27:29,189
Damn it.

266
00:27:29,272 --> 00:27:31,107
- [car lock beeps]
- Sabina, pick up.

267
00:27:35,195 --> 00:27:37,489
All aboard for Naga. All aboard!

268
00:27:37,572 --> 00:27:39,991
Bus for Naga now leaving. All aboard!

269
00:27:40,075 --> 00:27:43,244
All passengers traveling to Naga,
bus now leaving!

270
00:27:51,294 --> 00:27:53,296
[cell phone ringing]

271
00:27:57,717 --> 00:27:59,260
UNCLE ART

272
00:28:03,056 --> 00:28:04,391
[bus engine starts]

273
00:28:05,475 --> 00:28:07,310
[bus honks]

274
00:28:09,979 --> 00:28:12,482
- [Bulak] Wait! Please, wait!
- [conductor] Hold on. Where's your ticket?

275
00:28:12,565 --> 00:28:14,859
- [Bulak] I have money.
- [conductor] Okay, okay. There you go.

276
00:28:14,943 --> 00:28:17,612
Sorry, sorry. Excuse me. Sorry.

277
00:28:19,030 --> 00:28:22,242
[Bulak exhales deeply] Excuse me.
Excuse me. I'm with her.

278
00:28:24,744 --> 00:28:26,037
Thank you.

279
00:28:26,121 --> 00:28:27,705
Hey, what are you doing here?

280
00:28:27,789 --> 00:28:29,624
What? You thought
you could leave without me?

281
00:28:29,707 --> 00:28:31,000
Bulak, I'm serious.

282
00:28:31,084 --> 00:28:32,419
Yeah, I'm serious too.

283
00:28:32,502 --> 00:28:34,796
Only problem is
I didn't get a chance to pack.

284
00:28:34,879 --> 00:28:36,214
Good thing we're the same size.

285
00:28:37,257 --> 00:28:39,926
We don't know
what we're really gonna find there.

286
00:28:40,009 --> 00:28:42,220
What if Mom went someplace dangerous?

287
00:28:42,303 --> 00:28:43,680
That's why you'll need me.

288
00:28:45,223 --> 00:28:46,891
- Hey, you need to listen to--
- Just relax.

289
00:28:47,517 --> 00:28:48,935
It's okay. Chill.

290
00:28:51,146 --> 00:28:52,439
[Bulak sighs contentedly]

291
00:28:56,025 --> 00:28:57,736
[kisses]

292
00:29:14,878 --> 00:29:16,504
[bus honks]

293
00:29:29,350 --> 00:29:31,352
[ominous music playing]

294
00:29:44,616 --> 00:29:46,618
[crickets chirping]

295
00:30:16,606 --> 00:30:18,316
[music continues playing]

296
00:30:23,112 --> 00:30:24,906
[man groaning]

297
00:30:26,908 --> 00:30:29,744
[man whimpers]

298
00:30:32,789 --> 00:30:35,542
[man gasping]

299
00:30:36,417 --> 00:30:38,211
[man sobbing]

300
00:30:41,506 --> 00:30:44,175
[man screaming]

301
00:30:46,928 --> 00:30:49,430
- [flesh squelching]
- [axe clanking]

302
00:30:49,514 --> 00:30:51,516
[men cackling]

303
00:30:54,310 --> 00:30:56,062
[music grows darker]

304
00:31:24,340 --> 00:31:26,134
[insects trilling]

305
00:31:33,016 --> 00:31:35,143
[music crescendos]

306
00:31:47,196 --> 00:31:48,615
[brakes squeak]

307
00:31:57,916 --> 00:31:58,833
[Bulak] Thank you.

308
00:32:03,755 --> 00:32:05,757
[motorboat engine whirring]

309
00:32:07,467 --> 00:32:09,469
[mysterious music playing]

310
00:32:35,620 --> 00:32:37,038
[Sabina breathes deeply]

311
00:32:47,048 --> 00:32:49,968
- [Sabrina] 30,000.
- [Bulak] Babe, that's too much.

312
00:32:52,762 --> 00:32:55,098
You don't know about Babang Yawa, do you?

313
00:32:55,181 --> 00:32:56,516
Where'd you get that information?

314
00:32:56,599 --> 00:32:57,517
The Internet?

315
00:32:57,600 --> 00:32:58,643
All right then, 50.

316
00:32:58,726 --> 00:33:00,144
- [boatman] Fifty?
- Hey, babe.

317
00:33:00,228 --> 00:33:01,813
There are three of us here, you know,

318
00:33:01,896 --> 00:33:06,234
and another thing,
there is no island there in Babang Yawa.

319
00:33:06,317 --> 00:33:07,735
If that's where your mother went,

320
00:33:07,819 --> 00:33:09,696
then you'll never see her again.

321
00:33:10,613 --> 00:33:13,116
Come on, babe.
There's nothing that we can do now.

322
00:33:27,588 --> 00:33:28,923
[Sabina] <i>You know how to swim, right?</i>

323
00:33:34,387 --> 00:33:35,388
Stupid, I know.

324
00:33:35,972 --> 00:33:37,056
But I'm desperate.

325
00:33:38,683 --> 00:33:40,852
Yeah, well,
swimming doesn't make much sense.

326
00:33:40,935 --> 00:33:43,563
They say even airplanes
have disappeared there.

327
00:33:45,064 --> 00:33:46,232
You believe that?

328
00:33:46,315 --> 00:33:49,318
Well, I guess <i>they</i> do,
or there'd be someone to take us.

329
00:33:50,111 --> 00:33:53,239
Hey, let's just dance and eat. Here.

330
00:33:54,323 --> 00:33:56,409
I'm running out of ideas right now.

331
00:34:01,831 --> 00:34:03,249
There is another option.

332
00:34:05,084 --> 00:34:06,002
We leave.

333
00:34:08,296 --> 00:34:10,256
You can go. I'm staying.

334
00:34:10,339 --> 00:34:12,258
- Oh, fuck you.
- [Sabina chuckles]

335
00:34:13,551 --> 00:34:15,678
I'd be a real loser if I just leave you.

336
00:34:17,305 --> 00:34:18,222
Agreed.

337
00:34:19,515 --> 00:34:23,352
So, do you want me to go home
because you're tired of me?

338
00:34:26,606 --> 00:34:29,233
It's impossible for me to be tired of you.

339
00:34:30,068 --> 00:34:32,195
[giggles] Come on, eat.

340
00:34:35,490 --> 00:34:36,407
Here.

341
00:34:37,658 --> 00:34:38,659
Come on.

342
00:34:38,743 --> 00:34:41,662
You can't swim
if you're hungry. [chuckles]

343
00:34:44,457 --> 00:34:46,375
[both laugh softly]

344
00:34:47,668 --> 00:34:49,378
- Hey, you two.
- [Bulak] Sarge!

345
00:34:49,462 --> 00:34:52,048
You're not really planning to swim there?

346
00:34:52,632 --> 00:34:54,383
You know, I may look disorganized,

347
00:34:54,467 --> 00:34:57,303
but I do know
when something goes missing from my stuff.

348
00:35:00,515 --> 00:35:01,349
Huh?

349
00:35:02,308 --> 00:35:03,392
What's up with her?

350
00:35:04,852 --> 00:35:06,479
You seriously don't know?

351
00:35:06,562 --> 00:35:08,147
No doubt she's really mad at you.

352
00:35:08,856 --> 00:35:10,399
I'd be mad at you too.

353
00:35:10,483 --> 00:35:14,946
Whatever information I hid from her,
it was for her own good, you know?

354
00:35:16,364 --> 00:35:17,865
You still hid it.

355
00:35:17,949 --> 00:35:21,077
Now that she knows
where her mother might be, what now?

356
00:35:21,160 --> 00:35:22,370
I want to know her plans.

357
00:35:25,790 --> 00:35:26,791
Swimming.

358
00:35:30,002 --> 00:35:31,337
[lighter clicking]

359
00:35:33,798 --> 00:35:35,216
[boatman] Hey!

360
00:35:35,299 --> 00:35:36,509
Looking for a boat?

361
00:35:37,969 --> 00:35:39,804
Can that take me to Babang Yawa?

362
00:35:41,472 --> 00:35:44,016
Not this one. There, that one.

363
00:35:45,768 --> 00:35:46,602
How much?

364
00:35:47,186 --> 00:35:48,604
30,000, round trip.

365
00:35:48,688 --> 00:35:50,773
Ah, you offered Mando 50,000.

366
00:35:51,566 --> 00:35:52,859
Okay, 50,000.

367
00:35:54,443 --> 00:35:55,862
50,000 one way.

368
00:35:58,030 --> 00:35:59,448
No deal. Good luck.

369
00:36:00,783 --> 00:36:01,784
[Sabina] Wait!

370
00:36:03,244 --> 00:36:04,328
Hey, wait a minute.

371
00:36:07,165 --> 00:36:08,374
[Arturo] Sabina. Sabina.

372
00:36:09,333 --> 00:36:10,501
I'll take care of this.

373
00:36:13,588 --> 00:36:14,589
Sir.

374
00:36:17,383 --> 00:36:19,886
Let's talk about
how we might go about this.

375
00:36:27,643 --> 00:36:28,769
It's settled.

376
00:36:30,229 --> 00:36:31,772
Round trip, 30,000.

377
00:36:34,901 --> 00:36:36,903
[suspenseful music playing]

378
00:37:13,981 --> 00:37:16,901
Everything you now know, Sabina,
that's all I know too.

379
00:37:19,862 --> 00:37:23,199
But I had to steal from you
to find out what it was that you knew.

380
00:37:23,282 --> 00:37:24,492
That's the thing.

381
00:37:26,827 --> 00:37:28,329
You and Mom are both alike.

382
00:37:30,373 --> 00:37:32,500
You still both think I'm a child.

383
00:37:34,418 --> 00:37:37,630
I think that
you're exactly like your mother.

384
00:37:39,340 --> 00:37:42,635
If you'd known everything,
nothing would have stopped you.

385
00:37:42,718 --> 00:37:44,345
You're stubborn, just like her.

386
00:37:44,929 --> 00:37:47,640
Except you're more careless.

387
00:37:47,723 --> 00:37:49,517
More impatient.

388
00:37:49,600 --> 00:37:51,686
Planning to swim to Babang Yawa?

389
00:37:51,769 --> 00:37:53,396
You don't understand anything.

390
00:37:53,479 --> 00:37:55,523
Oh, yeah? Then explain it to me, huh?

391
00:37:57,441 --> 00:37:59,944
I've always had dreams about this island.

392
00:38:01,195 --> 00:38:03,281
I told my mom about it once.

393
00:38:03,364 --> 00:38:06,701
Then something started troubling her,
making her kind of crazy.

394
00:38:06,784 --> 00:38:09,662
- You should have told me about this.
- And then what?

395
00:38:13,040 --> 00:38:16,460
It seems you disappeared too, Uncle Art,
same time as Mom.

396
00:38:22,341 --> 00:38:26,637
I understand why it's scary,
and I know why you kept me in the dark.

397
00:38:26,721 --> 00:38:29,473
I don't need you to apologize or anything.

398
00:38:29,557 --> 00:38:33,602
I'm actually way past that,
but I'm still pissed at you.

399
00:38:41,235 --> 00:38:43,195
[coughs, retches]

400
00:38:43,279 --> 00:38:44,363
[Sabina] Bulak.

401
00:38:45,406 --> 00:38:46,741
- [coughs]
- Babe.

402
00:38:47,491 --> 00:38:49,118
- [retches, coughs]
- Here.

403
00:38:51,829 --> 00:38:53,581
- Are you okay?
- [sighs]

404
00:38:54,206 --> 00:38:55,416
Yeah, okay.

405
00:38:56,667 --> 00:38:59,837
You should check on Uncle Art.
Who knows how he's handling this?

406
00:39:06,927 --> 00:39:07,928
[chuckles softly]

407
00:39:18,606 --> 00:39:19,982
[boatman] Okay, we're here.

408
00:39:21,776 --> 00:39:23,152
[Bulak] Where is <i>here?</i>

409
00:39:23,235 --> 00:39:25,404
Babang Yawa. That's what we agreed.

410
00:39:25,488 --> 00:39:27,031
This is Babang Yawa?

411
00:39:27,114 --> 00:39:29,950
- What were you expecting?
- [Sabina] An island.

412
00:39:30,034 --> 00:39:31,494
Don't make fun of us, man.

413
00:39:31,577 --> 00:39:34,663
- This is the middle of the ocean.
- This is it.

414
00:39:34,747 --> 00:39:38,250
If you don't want to believe it,
then there's nothing I can do.

415
00:39:38,334 --> 00:39:39,877
This is as far as I can take you.

416
00:39:39,960 --> 00:39:42,505
[Arturo]
Just take us back to the pier right now.

417
00:39:42,588 --> 00:39:43,714
30,000.

418
00:39:43,798 --> 00:39:45,966
Listen, I already gave you the money.

419
00:39:46,050 --> 00:39:48,594
That was one way.
The return trip is another 30.

420
00:39:48,677 --> 00:39:51,138
Fuck you, dude! What sort of game is this?

421
00:39:51,222 --> 00:39:54,642
If we don't give it to you,
then how are you planning to return?

422
00:39:54,725 --> 00:39:57,853
I know she's got more money.
Hey! Don't you touch me.

423
00:39:57,937 --> 00:39:59,647
You think I'm scared of you?

424
00:39:59,730 --> 00:40:01,524
You think I can't handle you
'cause you're a cop?

425
00:40:01,607 --> 00:40:04,026
If I was gonna behave like a cop,
I'd pull this out.

426
00:40:04,110 --> 00:40:05,111
Ah, yeah, give it to me.

427
00:40:05,194 --> 00:40:07,446
- Sarge. Sarge, Sarge!
- Uncle!

428
00:40:09,156 --> 00:40:10,116
[grunts]

429
00:40:12,243 --> 00:40:14,036
[both men grunting]

430
00:40:14,120 --> 00:40:15,621
Uncle! Uncle!

431
00:40:15,704 --> 00:40:17,581
No! [screams]

432
00:40:18,624 --> 00:40:19,708
[Bulak] Don't… Sarge!

433
00:40:20,292 --> 00:40:21,377
Stop, stop, stop!

434
00:40:22,420 --> 00:40:24,839
- Be careful, be careful!
- [men yell]

435
00:40:24,922 --> 00:40:26,132
[grunts]

436
00:40:27,049 --> 00:40:28,717
Sabina, stay back!

437
00:40:28,801 --> 00:40:30,511
- [boatman grunts]
- Sabina!

438
00:40:30,594 --> 00:40:32,221
- [both grunt]
- [Bulak] Sabina!

439
00:40:32,304 --> 00:40:33,472
Babe, are you okay?

440
00:40:33,556 --> 00:40:35,766
- [groans]
- [weapon clatters]

441
00:40:38,394 --> 00:40:40,187
Bulak! Bulak!

442
00:40:40,271 --> 00:40:42,606
- [boatman grunting]
- [Sabina] Bulak!

443
00:40:42,690 --> 00:40:43,774
- [Sabina] Bulak!
- [Bulak] Sarge!

444
00:40:43,858 --> 00:40:45,484
- Stop struggling.
- Bulak!

445
00:40:45,568 --> 00:40:46,986
- Sarge.
- Stop it! You hear?

446
00:40:47,069 --> 00:40:50,281
- You're a filthy cheating scoundrel!
- [Bulak] Stop! You're gonna kill him.

447
00:40:50,364 --> 00:40:51,657
[boatman straining]

448
00:40:51,740 --> 00:40:52,825
[Arturo] What?

449
00:40:53,909 --> 00:40:55,828
Babang Yawa. There, there.

450
00:40:55,911 --> 00:40:57,955
[boat creaking]

451
00:41:04,420 --> 00:41:06,422
[ominous music playing]

452
00:41:09,341 --> 00:41:11,343
[boat continues creaking]

453
00:41:19,602 --> 00:41:21,896
[music grows darker]

454
00:41:22,980 --> 00:41:24,982
[wind howling]

455
00:41:29,862 --> 00:41:32,865
[waves crashing loudly]

456
00:41:32,948 --> 00:41:34,950
[wind howling]

457
00:41:37,578 --> 00:41:39,580
[breathing heavily]

458
00:41:41,248 --> 00:41:43,250
[waves crashing loudly]

459
00:41:51,842 --> 00:41:53,844
[rumbling]

460
00:42:06,607 --> 00:42:08,609
[sinister music playing]

461
00:42:21,163 --> 00:42:23,499
[water bubbling]

462
00:42:24,667 --> 00:42:25,501
[creaks]

463
00:42:25,584 --> 00:42:27,545
[creature howls]

464
00:42:35,344 --> 00:42:37,346
[ominous music playing]

465
00:43:10,462 --> 00:43:11,463
[squelches]

466
00:43:37,197 --> 00:43:40,075
[music crescendos]

467
00:43:41,201 --> 00:43:43,203
[theme music playing]
